  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nStill no real evidence of any cooler or wetter weather in the long-\nrange period. Troughing across the West Coast remains through the \nearly part of next week, but with the ridge centered over the Gulf \nCoast we will likely remain on the periphery/just outside of any \nsouthwesterly flow aloft and rain chances. While heat similar to \nThursday doesn't look likely to recur, air temperatures should still \nget up into the 100s across the entire area on most days. Fire \nweather will also likely be problematic at least one, if not all, of \nthe days in the long term, and that pattern will continue until the \nmoment we get a good soaking rain again.\n\nMeister",
